/* nbh-video-steps.js (v25.72): the Steps of each procedure video, for its page in the video library (videos.html).
   Each video has its step list and its captions drawn into the picture; this file holds the same words, as text, so the
   page can list the steps, mark the one playing with its caption, and jump to a step. Nothing here is about a student.
   steps: [number, start in seconds, title], every step the picture's own panel lists, with the panel's numbers and titles,
   in the order the video plays them, then "Before you start" (number 0, the closing card) last. A step the video does not
   play as a part of its own has a fourth item: 'open' (only on the opening card; its start is the card's, 0), 'close'
   (only on the closing card; its start is that card's), or 'with' and the number of the step it is shown with (its start
   is that step's). Those are never marked as the step playing. The FCT guide's panel shows steps 3 to 10; its steps 1
   and 2 are on its opening card, in the card's words.
   caps: [start in seconds, caption, step number] for every caption in the video, in order ('' with null: the opening
   card; 'Before you start' with 0: the closing card). A start is the first tenth of a second at which the caption is on
   the picture.
   Every title and caption is word for word what the picture shows: checked by drawing each one again in the video's
   own frame and comparing it with the video's picture at that second. */
